  "slug": "trees-phylogenetic-d93f",
  "summary": "New tools supply ground-truth simulation and annotation quality scoring, while a C. elegans pangenome shows what gene-content variation benchmarks must capture.",
  "synthesis": "The items address different problems, but the dominant thread is infrastructure for evaluating and interpreting gene-level comparative data. OrthoSimulator generates empirically calibrated datasets with known orthogroups and gene trees, giving ground truth for orthology inference benchmarks. ABAQS scores genome annotation quality through completeness, gene model validity and protein profile accuracy, and is applied to more than 1700 fungal genomes. On the biological side, the 140-strain C. elegans pangenome reveals extensive gene copy-number variation in hyper-divergent regions, and WormIE integrates multi-source C. elegans annotations for gene-list and RNA-seq interpretation. What is new is pairing explicit truth or quality metrics with resources that expose gene-content variation, so annotation and orthology methods can be validated against realistic complexity.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
